  "decision": "Reduce the $5K estimate from 58% to 56% and the $10K estimate from 27% to 26%. Five consecutive U.S. spot ETH ETF outflow sessions removed $431.4M through October 30, so institutional scores fall from 0.62 to 0.57 for $5K and from 0.45 to 0.40 for $10K while remaining yellow. ETH's October 31 stored snapshot is $2,244.71 (+1.1% over 24 hours), still below the lost $2.7K base after the Binance-driven two-month low. Binance says it reserved more than $6.34B against the reported $6.3B incident, but withdrawals remain suspended, additional breach points were found and independent proof of reserves is pending; market scores therefore fall from 0.38 to 0.26 for $5K and from 0.19 to 0.12 for $10K while remaining red. Rounded weighted signals become 52/37. Macro scores remain near their existing floor because sticky inflation, Brent near $116 and Hormuz risk reinforce rather than newly redefine the already-red regime. The probability reductions are deliberately smaller than October 8's regime change because no catalyst color changes and Binance states it has loss coverage; successful withdrawals, proof of reserves and a full post-mortem remain unverified."
